      "content": "Framing the upgrade as an insurance policy against business interruption rather than just a security fix can make abstract risks feel immediate. Present data showing how low-cost, routine threats (like supply chain vulnerabilities or insider risks) bypass their static defenses and cause severe downtime that even a perfect audit would miss. Use a \"what-if\" scenario demonstrating that a 1% increase in attack complexity over the next year would render their current perfect score worthless without advanced monitoring.",
